====================================================================================================
(3) THE DECISION: does the rising-share signature (NEGATIVE rho --
    share falls as the field rises) survive the partial/fixed-radius
    tests at rho > 0.3-class?
====================================================================================================
  bar: |rho| >= 0.25 (0.3-class) AND p < 0.05.
  pooled partial (control log10 r): rho = +0.626, p = 1.227e-11
  pooled partial (log r + cluster dummies): rho = +0.117, p = 2.906e-01
  pooled shell-wise Spearman (8 x 12): rho = +0.672, p = 4.975e-12; 5-band: rho = +0.540, p = 5.369e-08
  raw (G094) pooled rho for reference: -0.298 (p = 3.242e-03); the radius trend rho(s, log r) = +0.926
  DECISION (committed V4 share): INVERTED: net of radius the share-vs-field relation is significant at 0.3-class but POSITIVE -- at fixed radius the share is HIGHER where the field (and the cluster mass) is higher, the OPPOSITE of the V4 claim; the claimed negative signature was the radius confound, and the surviving field-driven component runs the other way
  DECISION (physical share, G106's s = rho_ph/rho_res): PARTIALLY SURVIVES on the PHYSICAL share: one reading stays 0.3-class significant, sign negative (claimed direction); the other collapses

====================================================================================================
(4) THE VERDICTS
====================================================================================================
  V1 the partial correlation: pooled rho(s, g/a0 | log10 r) = +0.626, p = 1.227e-11, n = 96, df = 93 (| r/R500 = +0.382, p = 1.313e-04; | both = +0.591, p = 3.570e-10; | log r + cluster dummies (within-cluster) = +0.117, p = 2.906e-01); per-cluster partials: 8/12 degenerate (curvature noise at n = 8); non-degenerate median -0.166, Fisher-pooled -0.160 (p = 4.704e-01)
  V2 the fixed-shell correlation: pooled shell-wise Spearman = +0.672, p = 4.975e-12 (8 shells x 12, Fisher-z, Q = 5.5, I^2 = 0%); median shell rho = +0.643 (0/8 negative); jackknife range [+0.595, +0.806]; share factors: dlnM piece -0.516 (p = 1.3e-06), mb/Mres piece +0.784 (p = 3.5e-19); 5-band grouping +0.540 (p = 5.369e-08)
  V3 the honest statement: INVERTED: net of radius the share-vs-field relation is significant at 0.3-class but POSITIVE -- at fixed radius the share is HIGHER where the field (and the cluster mass) is higher, the OPPOSITE of the V4 claim; the claimed negative signature was the radius confound, and the surviving field-driven component runs the other way.  The numbers that decide: raw pooled rho = -0.298 (p = 3.242e-03) riding on rho(s, log r) = +0.926 (p = 1.4e-41) and rho(log g, log r) = -0.537; with log10 r controlled, rho_partial = +0.626 (p = 1.227e-11); at fixed radius, pooled shell rho = +0.672 (p = 4.975e-12).  Physical-share lane (G106's s = rho_ph/rho_res): PARTIALLY SURVIVES on the PHYSICAL share: one reading stays 0.3-class significant, sign negative (claimed direction); the other collapses (pooled partial -0.283, p = 5.529e-03; pooled shell rho -0.170, p = 1.451e-01).

